The Darwin 26 MAC hook mpo_vnode_notify_end_rename_swap (mac_policy_ops slot 55, mpo_reserved16 in xnu-12377).
macOS 27's Sandbox locks the labels of both vnodes in its begin_rename_swap hook (slot 58, will_rename_swap here) and
unlocks them in end_rename_swap. xnu-12377 never called slot 55, so renamex_np(RENAME_SWAP) (launchd's dirs_cleaner
boot task) returned to user space holding both label locks and the kernel panicked. The end hook now runs once vn_rename
returns, whatever its result.
